// The counter-proof of the case beside it: if the body's last expression decided the block's
// value, this would be an `int` and the return type would be right. The block is a function, so
// the return type here is wrong and the program must be refused -- that refusal is what says the
// body's last expression is not what the block hands over.
func value_is_not_the_body(f: (x: float) => float) => int {
    return edit d = f { 42 }
}